Let an interrupted thunk be forced again on Determinate Nix.

Upstream 5c4f498d3 (in 2.35) restores a thunk that an `Interrupted`
stopped, so a later force evaluates it again (nixidae/nixidae#634).
Determinate Nix forces a thunk through its own concurrent state
machine, which stores every exception as `Value::Failed`, an interrupt
included. So a cancelled huggorm call poisoned the value for good:
test_an_interrupted_value_evaluates_again raised `Interrupted` again.

The thunk is restored when this thread owns it and no other thread
waits on it: the pending word swaps back to the thunk. A waiter needs a
final value, so a thunk another thread awaits fails as before.

Applies after nix-determinate-failed-value-releases-its-error.
